  ✓ CONFIRMED: Spot-price manipulation of concentrated LP collateral passes
    Justification: Upon reviewing V3Oracle.getValue, V3Oracle._getAmounts, 
V3Oracle._checkPoolPrice, and V3Vault._checkLoanIsHealthy/borrow, I confirmed 
that the hypothesized spot-price manipulation path exists. In 
V3Oracle._initializeState and _getAmounts, the position’s token amounts are 
calculated from pool.slot0().sqrtPriceX96, making collateral composition 
dependent on the current Uniswap V3 spot price. Although getValue obtains token 
prices from configured Chainlink/TWAP sources, its anti-manipulation check 
derives an oracle pool price from those same prices and compares it against 
_getReferencePoolPriceX96(pool, 0), which explicitly reads the manipulable 
current slot0 price rather than a TWAP. _requireMaxDifference only rejects 
deviations at or above the configurable maxPoolPriceDifference, with a minimum 
configuration of 2%, so a temporary price movement below the threshold is 
accepted while still changing the LP amounts and resulting collateral valuation.
V3Vault.borrow invokes _requireLoanIsHealthy using this valuation, allowing debt
to be increased during the manipulated state. Restoring the pool price afterward
does not undo the debt, and no independent spot/TWAP guard or valuation haircut 
prevents this path.


